        "\n",
        "**Check and prepare the data**\n",
        "Before clustering, we check for problems that would distort the groups:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **Missing values**: rows with gaps are set aside and listed, so they can be fixed at source.\n",
        "2. **Impossible values**: for example, tribes outside 0 to 3, or activity dates after the report date.\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **New joiners**: villagers with under six months' tenure have had less time to complete quests, so they are analysed separately.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "FRN-O9axAvts"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "FEATURES = [\"quests_completed_6m\", \"missions_joined_6m\", \"days_since_last_activity\", \"tribes_joined\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "missing = df[df[FEATURES].isna().any(axis=1)]\n",
        "invalid = df[(df[\"tribes_joined\"] < 0) | (df[\"tribes_joined\"] > 3) |\n",
        "             (df[\"quests_completed_6m\"] < 0) | (df[\"missions_joined_6m\"] < 0) |\n",
        "             (df[\"days_since_last_activity\"] < 0)]\n",
        "new_joiners = df[df[\"tenure_months\"] < 6]\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Rows with missing values: {len(missing)}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Rows with impossible values: {len(invalid)}\")\n",
        "print(f\"New joiners (under 6 months): {len(new_joiners)}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "excluded = set(missing.index) | set(invalid.index) | set(new_joiners.index)\n",
        "model_df = df.drop(index=list(excluded)).copy()\n",
        "print(f\"Villagers used for clustering: {len(model_df)}\")"
